  "modified": "2024-11-13T18:44:52Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: Improper type casting in calculation in palm.c could lead\n     to undefined behavior in processing input file\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-27761.patch: fix color calculation issue that\n       caused incorrect output when writing PALM images\n     - CVE-2020-27761\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Negative Quantum value handling issue in quantum-private.h\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-27757.patch: fix improper handling of negative\n       Quantum values\n     - CVE-2020-27757\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Excessive shifting overflow in quantum-export.c\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-27751.patch: fix shift exponent being too\n        large for 64-bit type in scaling function\n     - CVE-2020-27751\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Unsigned int type range issue at quantum-private.h\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-27768.patch: fix incorrect checking of\n       Quantum in quantum-private.h scaling functions\n     - CVE-2020-27768\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Unsigned char overflow in RestoreMSCWarning()\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-27771.patch: fix incorrect casting of\n     GetPixelIndex causing overflow\n     - CVE-2020-27771",
